			},
			solution: {
				'index.html': `<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{title}}<\/title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  <\/head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header" id="top">
      <p class="brand">{{name}}<\/p>
      <nav aria-label="Site sections">
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#sec-1">{{sections.0}}<\/a><\/li>
          <li><a href="#sec-2">{{sections.1}}<\/a><\/li>
          <li><a href="#sec-3">{{sections.2}}<\/a><\/li>
        <\/ul>
      <\/nav>
    <\/header>

    <main id="main">
      <h1>{{name}}<\/h1>
      <p>{{who}}<\/p>
      <p><a class="button" href="#inquiry">{{mainAction.label}}<\/a><\/p>

      <section id="sec-1">
        <h2>{{sections.0}}<\/h2>
        <p>A couple of sentences about this section.<\/p>
      <\/section>

      <section id="sec-2">
        <h2>{{sections.1}}<\/h2>
        <p>A couple of sentences about this section.<\/p>
      <\/section>

      <section id="sec-3">
        <h2>{{sections.2}}<\/h2>
        <p>A couple of sentences about this section.<\/p>
      <\/section>

      <section id="offer">
        <h2>What we offer<\/h2>
        <div class="cards">
          {{#each items}}<article class="card">
            <h3>{{title}}<\/h3>
            <p>{{text}}<\/p>
            <p class="price">{{price}}<\/p>
          <\/article>
          {{/each}}
        <\/div>
      <\/section>

      <section id="inquiry">
        <h2>{{mainAction.label}}<\/h2>
        <form action="/inquiry" method="post">
          <p>
            <label for="f-name">What should we call you?<\/label><br>
            <input id="f-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required>
          <\/p>
          <p>
            <label for="f-phone">Phone<\/label><br>
            <input id="f-phone" name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" required>
          <\/p>
          <p><button type="submit">{{mainAction.label}}<\/button><\/p>
        <\/form>
      <\/section>
    <\/main>

    <section data-scaffold id="register">
      <h2>The project’s data register<\/h2>
      <p>For each group of data: what it is, why you hold it, where it sits, how long it is kept and on what condition it is deleted, who has access, the lawful basis, and whether it is personal data.<\/p>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Data<\/th><th>Purpose<\/th><th>Where it is stored<\/th><th>Retention and deletion<\/th><th>Who has access<\/th><th>Lawful basis<\/th><th>Personal data?<\/th><\/tr>
        <tr class="field visitor"><td class="what">Visitor’s name from the request form<\/td><td class="why">to know how to address them when replying<\/td><td class="where">the requests table in PostgreSQL, on a server in the United States<\/td><td class="keep">3 years after the request, then a script deletes it<\/td><td class="access">the owner through the admin screen, and the site’s server<\/td><td class="basis">steps the person asked for (replying to a request)<\/td><td class="pd">yes<\/td><\/tr>
        <tr class="field visitor"><td class="what">Visitor’s phone number<\/td><td class="why">to get in touch about the request, and for nothing else<\/td><td class="where">the requests table in PostgreSQL, on a server in the United States<\/td><td class="keep">3 years after the request, then a script deletes it<\/td><td class="access">the owner through the admin screen, and the site’s server<\/td><td class="basis">steps the person asked for (replying to a request)<\/td><td class="pd">yes<\/td><\/tr>
        <tr class="field visitor"><td class="what">Comment on the request (free text)<\/td><td class="why">to understand the task before the call<\/td><td class="where">the requests table in PostgreSQL, on a server in the United States<\/td><td class="keep">1 year after the request, then deleted<\/td><td class="access">the owner through the admin screen<\/td><td class="basis">steps the person asked for (replying to a request)<\/td><td class="pd">yes, if the person writes about themselves<\/td><\/tr>
        <tr class="field people"><td class="what">Data of the people you show on the site (people)<\/td><td class="why">so that visitors know who they will work with<\/td><td class="where">the people table and a page of the site, on a server in the United States<\/td><td class="keep">while the person works on the project, then deleted at their request<\/td><td class="access">the owner and the person themselves<\/td><td class="basis">the person’s consent to be shown<\/td><td class="pd">yes: name and photo, published with the person’s consent<\/td><\/tr>
      <\/table>
      <p>A field I decided not to collect although I was tempted, and why: <span id="removed">date of birth: a consultation request does not need it, and it would only add personal data<\/span><\/p>
      <p>Where the main record of visitors’ data sits, and what happens to copies or transfers to another country: <span id="localisation">the main record of requests goes into a database on a server in the United States, where my visitors are; there are no copies abroad, and if one appears it is a transfer that needs a safeguard (standard contractual clauses), which I would settle with an attorney first<\/span><\/p>
      <p>How personal data is kept apart from the rest in the schema: <span id="separate">requests sit in a table of their own called requests, and logs and analytics keep only the request number, without a name or phone<\/span><\/p>

      <h3>Consent as a record in the database<\/h3>
      <textarea aria-label="Consent as a record in the database" id="q-consent" rows="9">CREATE TABLE consents (
  id serial PRIMARY KEY,
  request_id integer REFERENCES requests(id),
  given_at timestamp NOT NULL,
  text_version text NOT NULL,
  purpose text NOT NULL
);<\/textarea>
    <\/section>


    <footer class="site-footer">
      <p>{{name}}, {{city}}<\/p>
    <\/footer>
  <\/body>
<\/html>
`,
				'styles.css': `/* styles.css: the page after the CSS part, abridged */

